k=\"dark-menu-bar.png\" narrow alt=\"The Reclaim menu-bar window with free space, a storage bar, the last scan and Scan Now and Clean Saf…\" />"},"10":{"id":"/docs/automation-8","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#the-menu-bar","content":"**Free space** and a small storage bar, with what the last scan found."},"11":{"id":"/docs/automation-9","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#the-menu-bar","content":"**Scan Now** starts a scan without opening the window."},"12":{"id":"/docs/automation-10","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#the-menu-bar","content":"**Clean Safe Items** deletes every Safe suggestion Reclaim can delete, then shows a notification with the space freed."},"13":{"id":"/docs/automation-11","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#the-menu-bar","content":"**Open Reclaim**, Settings and Quit."},"14":{"id":"/docs/automation-12","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#the-menu-bar","content":"Hide it with Show Reclaim in the menu bar. Scheduled scans and alerts keep running while Reclaim is open, even with its window closed."},"15":{"id":"/docs/automation-13","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#scheduled-scans","content":"Choose **Every day** or **Every week** in Automation › Scan automatically. A scan runs when one is due, including right after your Mac wakes, and by default only sends a notification such as *“12.4 GB can be reclaimed, 3.1 GB of it Safe.”*"},"16":{"id":"/docs/automation-14","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#auto-clean","content":"Off by default, and the only time Reclaim deletes something nobody ticked at that moment. When **Delete Safe items untouched for a day** is on, each scheduled scan deletes:"},"17":{"id":"/docs/automation-15","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#auto-clean","content":"only <Level of=\"safe\" /> items, never Rebuild or Personal ones;"},"18":{"id":"/docs/automation-16","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#auto-clean","content":"only items you can delete without the helper;"},"19":{"id":"/docs/automation-17","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#auto-clean","content":"only items where nothing inside changed for 24 hours, so a project you are working in keeps its caches."},"20":{"id":"/docs/automation-18","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#auto-clean","content":"It follows your Trash setting, is recorded in the history, and a notification tells you what was freed."},"21":{"id":"/docs/automation-19","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#low-space-alerts","content":"Reclaim checks free space every few minutes and notifies you once when it drops below your threshold, 10 GB by default, and again only after it has recovered and dropped again."},"22":{"id":"/docs/automation-20","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#open-at-login","content":"Turn on **Open at login** in Automation so the menu bar and schedules are always running. If macOS asks you to approve it, Reclaim shows a button to **Login Items** in System Settings."},"23":{"id":"/docs/automation-21","page_id":"/docs/automation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/automation#notifications","content":"The first time you turn on a schedule or low-space alerts, macOS asks whether Reclaim may send notifications. You can change this later in **System Settings › Notifications**."},"24":{"id":"/docs/docker","page_id":"/docs/docker","type":"page","content":"Docker and OrbStack","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/docker"},"25":{"id":"/docs/docker-0","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker","content":"Free disk space used by Docker Desktop, OrbStack and Colima. Reclaim removes build cache, unused images, stopped containers and volumes with Docker's own commands."},"26":{"id":"/docs/docker-1","page_id":"/docs/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/docker#what-you-need","content":"What you need"},"27":{"id":"/docs/docker-2","page_id":"/docs/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/docker#what-is-listed","content":"What is listed"},"28":{"id":"/docs/docker-3","page_id":"/docs/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/docker#how-removal-works","content":"How removal works"},"29":{"id":"/docs/docker-4","page_id":"/docs/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/docker#about-the-sizes","content":"About the sizes"},"30":{"id":"/docs/docker-5","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#what-you-need","content":"The `docker` command and a running engine: **OrbStack**, **Docker Desktop**, **Colima** or another. Reclaim finds the command in the usual places, even when it is opened from Finder. Open **Containers** in the sidebar; if the engine is not running, start it and click **Refresh**."},"31":{"id":"/docs/docker-6","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#what-is-listed","content":"| Item        | What it is                                                 | Removed with                 | Level   |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- |\n| Build cache | Layers kept to speed up builds, not used by any image now. | `docker builder prune --all` | <Level of=\"safe\" /> |","table":"table-0"},"32":{"id":"/docs/docker-7","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#what-is-listed","content":"| Item           | What it is                                                     | Removed with      | Level   |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- | ------- |\n| Dangling image | An untagged image left behind when a newer build took its tag. | `docker image rm` | <Level of=\"safe\" /> |","table":"table-0"},"33":{"id":"/docs/docker-8","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#what-is-listed","content":"| Item         | What it is                                                           | Removed with      | Level   |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- | ------- |\n| Unused image | A tagged image no container uses. Pulled or built again when needed. | `docker image rm` | <Level of=\"rebuild\" /> |","table":"table-0"},"34":{"id":"/docs/docker-9","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#what-is-listed","content":"| Item              | What it is                                                        | Removed with          | Level   |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------- |\n| Stopped container | A container that is not running. Changes made inside it are lost. | `docker container rm` | <Level of=\"rebuild\" /> |","table":"table-0"},"35":{"id":"/docs/docker-10","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#what-is-listed","content":"| Item          | What it is                                              | Removed with       | Level   |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------- |\n| Unused volume | A volume no container uses. These often hold databases. | `docker volume rm` | <Level of=\"personal\" /> |","table":"table-0"},"36":{"id":"/docs/docker-11","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#what-is-listed","content":"Images, containers and volumes that are in use are never listed. Select a row to read what it is and what happens after removing it."},"37":{"id":"/docs/docker-12","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#how-removal-works","content":"<Callout type=\"success\">Ticked items are removed with Docker's own commands, never forced, so Docker itself refuses anything a container is using. Reclaim never touches the engine's disk image directly.</Callout>"},"38":{"id":"/docs/docker-13","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#how-removal-works","content":"Docker items share the Delete bar and the history with everything else. If Docker refuses an item, the summary shows Docker's reason and the item stays in the list."},"39":{"id":"/docs/docker-14","page_id":"/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/docker#about-the-sizes","content":"Sizes come from `docker system df`. For an image, Reclaim shows the space only that image uses, which is what removing it frees; layers shared with other images stay. Totals can differ slightly from Docker's own summary because Docker rounds each size it reports."},"40":{"id":"/docs/explore","page_id":"/docs/explore","type":"page","content":"Disk Map and duplicates","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/explore"},"41":{"id":"/docs/explore-0","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore","content":"See where your Mac's disk space went with a size-sorted Disk Map, find large files, and remove duplicate files with APFS clones handled correctly."},"42":{"id":"/docs/explore-1","page_id":"/docs/explore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explore#disk-map","content":"Disk Map"},"43":{"id":"/docs/explore-2","page_id":"/docs/explore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explore#large-files","content":"Large Files"},"44":{"id":"/docs/explore-3","page_id":"/docs/explore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explore#duplicates","content":"Duplicates"},"45":{"id":"/docs/explore-4","page_id":"/docs/explore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explore#how-duplicates-are-found","content":"How duplicates are found"},"46":{"id":"/docs/explore-5","page_id":"/docs/explore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explore#what-it-leaves-out","content":"What it leaves out"},"47":{"id":"/docs/explore-6","page_id":"/docs/explore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explore#hard-links-and-apfs-copies","content":"Hard links and APFS copies"},"48":{"id":"/docs/explore-7","page_id":"/docs/explore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explore#choosing-which-copy-to-keep","content":"Choosing which copy to keep"},"49":{"id":"/docs/explore-8","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#disk-map","content":"<Screenshot src=\"disk-map.png\" dark=\"dark-disk-map.png\" alt=\"The Disk Map listing folders with size bars, sizes, their share of the parent folder and file counts…\" />"},"50":{"id":"/docs/explore-9","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#disk-map","content":"The whole scan as folders and files, largest first. Each row has a bar for its share of the folder you are in, its size, the number of files inside and when anything in it last changed."},"51":{"id":"/docs/explore-10","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#disk-map","content":"**Go deeper:** double-click a folder, or right-click it and choose **Open**."},"52":{"id":"/docs/explore-11","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#disk-map","content":"**Go back:** click any folder in the trail at the top, or press ⌘ ↑."},"53":{"id":"/docs/explore-12","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#disk-map","content":"**Tick anything** that is not protected. Protected folders, such as the top level of the disk or your home folder, have a dimmed checkbox."},"54":{"id":"/docs/explore-13","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#disk-map","content":"**Badges** mark folders a rule already suggests. A lock means a folder could not be read, so its size is a lower bound."},"55":{"id":"/docs/explore-14","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#disk-map","content":"**Small files** under 1 MB are not listed one by one; their total appears below the list."},"56":{"id":"/docs/explore-15","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#large-files","content":"Files of 500 MB or more that no other suggestion covers. Files inside apps and photo libraries are left out, because deleting part of a bundle breaks it. Everything here is <Level of=\"personal\" />: only you know whether you still need it. Change the size in Scanning › Large files from."},"57":{"id":"/docs/explore-16","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#duplicates","content":"After a scan, open **Duplicates** and click **Find Duplicates**. Reclaim compares files of 1 MB or more and lists only files whose contents are identical, byte for byte."},"58":{"id":"/docs/explore-17","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#how-duplicates-are-found","content":"**By size.** Files with a unique size cannot have a twin, so they are dropped first."},"59":{"id":"/docs/explore-18","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#how-duplicates-are-found","content":"**By their edges.** The first and last 64 KB of the remaining files are compared."},"60":{"id":"/docs/explore-19","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#how-duplicates-are-found","content":"**By full contents.** Only the candidates left are read in full and compared by SHA-256. On a typical Mac this takes seconds."},"61":{"id":"/docs/explore-20","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#what-it-leaves-out","content":"Anything inside apps, libraries and other bundles."},"62":{"id":"/docs/explore-21","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#what-it-leaves-out","content":"Hidden folders such as `~/.vscode`, and installed packages such as `node_modules` and `site-packages`: copies there belong to tools, and deleting one can break them."},"63":{"id":"/docs/explore-22","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#what-it-leaves-out","content":"App and system data in `~/Library`, `/Library` and `/Users/Shared`."},"64":{"id":"/docs/explore-23","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#what-it-leaves-out","content":"Anything another suggestion already covers."},"65":{"id":"/docs/explore-24","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#hard-links-and-apfs-copies","content":"**Hard links** are one file with several names, so they never appear as duplicates. **APFS copies**, such as those made with Finder's Duplicate, can share storage with the original. Reclaim detects them from where their data sits on disk and marks them *Shares storage*. Deleting one frees almost nothing, so they don't count towards the reclaimable total."},"66":{"id":"/docs/explore-25","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#choosing-which-copy-to-keep","content":"Nothing is ticked for you. The **Keep** menu in the toolbar ticks all but one copy in every group shown:"},"67":{"id":"/docs/explore-26","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#choosing-which-copy-to-keep","content":"**Keep Oldest Copy** or **Keep Newest Copy**, by modification date."},"68":{"id":"/docs/explore-27","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#choosing-which-copy-to-keep","content":"**Keep the Copy in a Folder…**: in groups with a copy in the folder you choose, that copy is kept."},"69":{"id":"/docs/explore-28","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#choosing-which-copy-to-keep","content":"**Untick All Copies**."},"70":{"id":"/docs/explore-29","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#choosing-which-copy-to-keep","content":"Filter first to apply Keep to only some groups. Right-click a copy for **Keep Only This Copy**."},"71":{"id":"/docs/explore-30","page_id":"/docs/explore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explore#choosing-which-copy-to-keep","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">If every copy in a group is ticked, the group shows a warning: deleting them all leaves you with none.</Callout>"},"72":{"id":"/docs/faq","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"page","content":"FAQ","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq"},"73":{"id":"/docs/faq-0","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"Answers about Reclaim for Mac, covering why there is no confirmation, protected folders, sizes compared with Finder, Full Disk Access, the root helper and privacy."},"74":{"id":"/docs/faq-1","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#safety","content":"Safety"},"75":{"id":"/docs/faq-2","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-is-there-no-are-you-sure","content":"Why is there no \"Are you sure?\""},"76":{"id":"/docs/faq-3","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#will-reclaim-ever-delete-things-on-its-own","content":"Will Reclaim ever delete things on its own?"},"77":{"id":"/docs/faq-4","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-undo-a-deletion","content":"Can I undo a deletion?"},"78":{"id":"/docs/faq-5","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#is-it-safe-to-delete-safe-items-while-i-am-working","content":"Is it safe to delete Safe items while I am working?"},"79":{"id":"/docs/faq-6","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-was-something-not-deleted","content":"Why was something not deleted?"},"80":{"id":"/docs/faq-7","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#is-a-helper-that-runs-as-root-safe","content":"Is a helper that runs as root safe?"},"81":{"id":"/docs/faq-8","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#protected-folders","content":"Protected folders"},"82":{"id":"/docs/faq-9","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"83":{"id":"/docs/faq-10","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-do-reclaims-sizes-differ-from-finders","content":"Why do Reclaim's sizes differ from Finder's?"},"84":{"id":"/docs/faq-11","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-doesnt-free-space-go-up-by-exactly-what-i-deleted","content":"Why doesn't free space go up by exactly what I deleted?"},"85":{"id":"/docs/faq-12","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-doesnt-the-scan-total-match-the-used-space","content":"Why doesn't the scan total match the used space?"},"86":{"id":"/docs/faq-13","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#permissions","content":"Permissions"},"87":{"id":"/docs/faq-14","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-are-my-desktop-documents-and-downloads-missing-from-the-scan","content":"Why are my Desktop, Documents and Downloads missing from the scan?"},"88":{"id":"/docs/faq-15","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-does-it-need-full-disk-access","content":"Why does it need Full Disk Access?"},"89":{"id":"/docs/faq-16","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-isnt-it-in-the-mac-app-store","content":"Why isn't it in the Mac App Store?"},"90":{"id":"/docs/faq-17","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-does-macos-block-it-the-first-time","content":"Why does macOS block it the first time?"},"91":{"id":"/docs/faq-18","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#privacy","content":"Privacy"},"92":{"id":"/docs/faq-19","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#does-reclaim-send-anything-over-the-network","content":"Does Reclaim send anything over the network?"},"93":{"id":"/docs/faq-20","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-is-there-no-are-you-sure","content":"Because cleaning a developer Mac means deleting hundreds of items, and a confirmation for each one gets clicked through without reading. Instead, Reclaim explains every item before you tick it, ticks only Safe items for you, and refuses to delete protected folders at all. If you want a safety net, turn on Move to Trash."},"94":{"id":"/docs/faq-21","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#will-reclaim-ever-delete-things-on-its-own","content":"Only if you turn on auto-clean for scheduled scans, which is off by default. Even then it deletes only Safe items that nothing changed for 24 hours. See how auto-clean works."},"95":{"id":"/docs/faq-22","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-undo-a-deletion","content":"Not when deleting permanently, which is the default. With Move to Trash on, items go to the Trash and you can put them back from there until you empty it."},"96":{"id":"/docs/faq-23","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#is-it-safe-to-delete-safe-items-while-i-am-working","content":"Usually. Quit an app before deleting its cache, and stop a dev server before deleting its project's build cache. Otherwise the app may recreate files mid-way or show errors until restarted."},"97":{"id":"/docs/faq-24","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-was-something-not-deleted","content":"The summary after deleting gives the reason for each item. Most often the files belong to root, for example ones created with `sudo npm install`. Install the helper to delete those. Files macOS itself protects cannot be deleted by any app."},"98":{"id":"/docs/faq-25","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#is-a-helper-that-runs-as-root-safe","content":"It deletes only inside system cache and log folders and your own home folder, never a protected folder, and refuses tricks with `..` and symlinks. It only answers the exact copy of Reclaim that installed it. The source is public, and you can remove it any time from System."},"99":{"id":"/docs/faq-26","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#protected-folders","content":"These are never deleted as a whole, however the path is written: with different capital letters, through a symlink, or as `/System/Volumes/Data/…`. Everything inside them, apart from the system folders, can still be deleted."},"100":{"id":"/docs/faq-27","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#protected-folders","content":"The disk root, and every folder directly in it, such as `/Applications`, `/Library`, `/Users` and `/opt`."},"101":{"id":"/docs/faq-28","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#protected-folders","content":"Everything in `/System`, `/usr` (except `/usr/local`), `/bin` and `/sbin`."},"102":{"id":"/docs/faq-29","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#protected-folders","content":"The folders directly in `/private`, and system folders such as `/Library/Caches` and `/opt/homebrew`."},"103":{"id":"/docs/faq-30","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#protected-folders","content":"Every user's home folder, and every mounted volume in `/Volumes`."},"104":{"id":"/docs/faq-31","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#protected-folders","content":"In your home: Desktop, Documents, Downloads, Movies, Music, Pictures, Public, Applications, the Trash, Library, and Library's main folders such as Application Support, Caches, Containers and Preferences."},"105":{"id":"/docs/faq-32","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#protected-folders","content":"Separately, macOS itself stops any app from changing its system files."},"106":{"id":"/docs/faq-33","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-do-reclaims-sizes-differ-from-finders","content":"Reclaim shows the space files actually take on disk; Finder often shows how long files are. They differ for sparse files such as virtual-machine disks, which can claim 64 GB while using a few, and for small files, which still occupy at least one disk block. Hard-linked files are counted once."},"107":{"id":"/docs/faq-34","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-doesnt-free-space-go-up-by-exactly-what-i-deleted","content":"Files that were APFS copies of each other shared their storage; local Time Machine snapshots still hold the deleted data until macOS removes them; and macOS counts \"purgeable\" space as free. The figure settles within a few minutes."},"108":{"id":"/docs/faq-35","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-doesnt-the-scan-total-match-the-used-space","content":"Folders Reclaim cannot read are missing from the total (give it Full Disk Access), and the disk also holds snapshots and file-system data that are not files."},"109":{"id":"/docs/faq-36","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-are-my-desktop-documents-and-downloads-missing-from-the-scan","content":"Reclaim does not have Full Disk Access yet. Without it, macOS shows a permission dialog for each of those folders and holds the scan until you answer, so Reclaim skips them instead. Turn on Full Disk Access and scan again."},"110":{"id":"/docs/faq-37","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-does-it-need-full-disk-access","content":"macOS hides other apps' data, Mail, Messages and parts of your Library from apps by default. Without access, those folders are not measured or suggested. Reclaim works without it, but sees less."},"111":{"id":"/docs/faq-38","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-isnt-it-in-the-mac-app-store","content":"App Store apps run in a sandbox that cannot read or delete files across the disk, which is the whole point of Reclaim."},"112":{"id":"/docs/faq-39","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-does-macos-block-it-the-first-time","content":"The app is not notarized, which requires a paid Apple developer membership. Follow Open it the first time, or build it from source."},"113":{"id":"/docs/faq-40","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#does-reclaim-send-anything-over-the-network","content":"No. It has no account, no analytics and no update check. The scan and your file list stay on your Mac. Its only files are its settings and the deletion history."},"114":{"id":"/docs/guide","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"page","content":"Scan and clean","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide"},"115":{"id":"/docs/guide-0","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide","content":"How to scan your Mac with Reclaim, read the Overview, review suggestions by safety level, and delete caches, node_modules and other junk in one click."},"116":{"id":"/docs/guide-1","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide#scanning","content":"Scanning"},"117":{"id":"/docs/guide-2","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide#the-overview","content":"The Overview"},"118":{"id":"/docs/guide-3","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide#reviewing-suggestions","content":"Reviewing suggestions"},"119":{"id":"/docs/guide-4","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide#safety-levels","content":"Safety levels"},"120":{"id":"/docs/guide-5","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide#deleting","content":"Deleting"},"121":{"id":"/docs/guide-6","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide#history","content":"History"},"122":{"id":"/docs/guide-7","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"Keyboard shortcuts"},"123":{"id":"/docs/guide-8","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#scanning","content":"Click **Scan** on the Overview, or press ⌘ R. Reclaim reads every folder it is allowed to and shows a live count of files and bytes. A full Mac takes about a minute; click **Stop** at any time."},"124":{"id":"/docs/guide-9","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#scanning","content":"**Whole disk by default.** To scan only your home folder, change Scanning › Scan."},"125":{"id":"/docs/guide-10","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#scanning","content":"**Real sizes.** Reclaim counts the space files actually use. A 32 GB disk image holding 1 GB counts as 1 GB, and a file with several hard links counts once."},"126":{"id":"/docs/guide-11","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#scanning","content":"**One disk only.** External drives and other volumes are never scanned."},"127":{"id":"/docs/guide-12","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#scanning","content":"**Without Full Disk Access**, Desktop, Documents, Downloads, iCloud Drive and other apps' data are skipped, so macOS doesn't pause the scan to ask about each one. Turn it on."},"128":{"id":"/docs/guide-13","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#the-overview","content":"<Screenshot src=\"overview.png\" alt=\"Overview with a storage bar, the last scan's summary and the top categories.\" />"},"129":{"id":"/docs/guide-14","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#the-overview","content":"**Storage bar:** used space, the part Reclaim suggests deleting in your accent colour, and free space."},"130":{"id":"/docs/guide-15","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#the-overview","content":"**Last scan:** how much you could reclaim, how much of it is Safe, and how long the scan took."},"131":{"id":"/docs/guide-16","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#the-overview","content":"**Top categories:** each kind of suggestion with its size. Click one to open it."},"132":{"id":"/docs/guide-17","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#reviewing-suggestions","content":"The sidebar has one entry per kind of suggestion, with its total size. What it finds lists every rule. Each list shows a checkbox, the item's name and folder, its size, its safety level and when anything inside it last changed."},"133":{"id":"/docs/guide-18","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#reviewing-suggestions","content":"**Sort** by clicking a column header, and **filter** with the search field (⌘ F)."},"134":{"id":"/docs/guide-19","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#reviewing-suggestions","content":"**Select All Safe** ticks every Safe item in the list; **Deselect All** unticks the list."},"135":{"id":"/docs/guide-20","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#reviewing-suggestions","content":"**Right-click** rows to tick or untick several at once, or to reveal one in Finder."},"136":{"id":"/docs/guide-21","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#reviewing-suggestions","content":"**The inspector** on the right explains the selected item: what it is, why it is suggested, what happens after deleting it, and where it is."},"137":{"id":"/docs/guide-22","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#reviewing-suggestions","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">An orange warning next to an app's cache means that app is running; quit it before deleting its files. A lock means the item belongs to root, and deleting it needs the helper.</Callout>"},"138":{"id":"/docs/guide-23","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#safety-levels","content":"| Level   | Meaning                                                                                                | Ticked for you |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------- |\n| <Level of=\"safe\" /> | Rebuilds itself; nothing for you to do. Build caches, app caches, logs, emulator snapshots, the Trash. | Yes            |","table":"table-0"},"139":{"id":"/docs/guide-24","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#safety-levels","content":"| Level   | Meaning                                                                                | Ticked for you |\n| ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| <Level of=\"rebuild\" /> | Comes back after a reinstall or download, such as `npm install` or `composer install`. | No             |","table":"table-0"},"140":{"id":"/docs/guide-25","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#safety-levels","content":"| Level   | Meaning                                                                                            | Ticked for you |\n| ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| <Level of=\"personal\" /> | Your data, reported so you can decide: old downloads, large files, duplicates, emulator user data. | No             |","table":"table-0"},"141":{"id":"/docs/guide-26","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#safety-levels","content":"To stop Reclaim ticking Safe items after each scan, turn off Tick Safe items after each scan."},"142":{"id":"/docs/guide-27","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#deleting","content":"Whenever something is ticked, a bar at the bottom shows how many items and how much space, such as **Delete 23 items · 31.4 GB**. Ticks carry across every list, the Disk Map, Duplicates and Containers, and an item inside a ticked folder is never counted twice."},"143":{"id":"/docs/guide-28","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#deleting","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\" title=\"There is no confirmation\">The button, or ⌘ ⌫, deletes ticked items immediately and permanently. For a safety net, turn on Move to Trash instead of deleting permanently; space is then freed only when you empty the Trash.</Callout>"},"144":{"id":"/docs/guide-29","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#deleting","content":"A sheet shows progress, then a summary of what was freed and anything that could not be removed, with the reason:"},"145":{"id":"/docs/guide-30","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#deleting","content":"**Belongs to another user**, such as root: files created with `sudo` or by the system. The helper can delete these."},"146":{"id":"/docs/guide-31","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#deleting","content":"**It no longer exists:** something else removed it after the scan."},"147":{"id":"/docs/guide-32","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#deleting","content":"**Protected:** one of the folders Reclaim never deletes as a whole. See the FAQ."},"148":{"id":"/docs/guide-33","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#deleting","content":"Lists and the Disk Map update straight away; no rescan is needed."},"149":{"id":"/docs/guide-34","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#history","content":"Every run is recorded: when, what was deleted or moved to the Trash, its size and anything that failed. The log is kept at `~/Library/Application Support/Reclaim/history.jsonl`."},"150":{"id":"/docs/guide-35","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Shortcut | Action |\n| -------- | ------ |\n| ⌘ R      | Scan   |","table":"table-1"},"151":{"id":"/docs/guide-36","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Shortcut | Action                                    |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| ⌘ ⌫      | Delete ticked items, with no confirmation |","table":"table-1"},"152":{"id":"/docs/guide-37","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Shortcut | Action                  |\n| -------- | ----------------------- |\n| ⌘ F      | Filter the current list |","table":"table-1"},"153":{"id":"/docs/guide-38","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Shortcut | Action                           |\n| -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| ⌘ ↑      | Enclosing folder in the Disk Map |","table":"table-1"},"154":{"id":"/docs/guide-39","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide#keyboard-shortcuts","content":"| Shortcut | Action   |\n| -------- | -------- |\n| ⌘ ,      | Settings |","table":"table-1"},"155":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"156":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Reclaim is a free, open-source Mac app that finds build caches, dependencies, app caches and Docker leftovers, explains what is safe to delete, and frees the space in one click."},"157":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-makes-it-different","content":"What makes it different"},"158":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"159":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Developer Macs fill up quietly: `.next` and DerivedData folders, `node_modules` in every old project, Gradle and npm caches, emulator images, Docker build cache. Reclaim scans the whole disk, tells you what each of those is and what happens if you delete it, and removes what you tick in one click."},"160":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Install\" href=\"/docs/install\" description=\"Download, open it the first time, and give it Full Disk Access.\" />"},"161":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Scan and clean\" href=\"/docs/guide\" description=\"Your first scan, the safety levels, and deleting.\" />"},"162":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"What it finds\" href=\"/docs/what-it-finds\" description=\"Every rule, with its safety level.\" />"},"163":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"FAQ\" href=\"/docs/faq\" description=\"Safety, permissions, sizes and privacy.\" />"},"164":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-makes-it-different","content":"**It explains everything.** Every suggestion says what it is, why it is listed and what happens after you delete it."},"165":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-makes-it-different","content":"**Three safety levels.** <Level of=\"safe\" /> items rebuild themselves and are ticked for you. <Level of=\"rebuild\" /> and <Level of=\"personal\" /> items wait for your decision."},"166":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-makes-it-different","content":"**No nagging.** Tick, click, done, with a summary of anything that could not be removed."},"167":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-makes-it-different","content":"**Hard limits.** System folders, your home folder and folders like Documents are never deleted as a whole, however the path is written."},"168":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-makes-it-different","content":"**Private.** No account, no analytics, no network access. The source is on GitHub."},"169":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#requirements","content":"macOS 14 Sonoma or later, on Apple silicon or Intel."},"170":{"id":"/docs/install","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"page","content":"Install","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/install"},"171":{"id":"/docs/install-0","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install","content":"Download the Reclaim disk image for Mac, open it through Privacy & Security the first time, and give it Full Disk Access. Plus updating, uninstalling and building from source."},"172":{"id":"/docs/install-1","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#install-from-terminal","content":"Install from Terminal"},"173":{"id":"/docs/install-2","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#or-download-the-disk-image","content":"Or download the disk image"},"174":{"id":"/docs/install-3","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#get-the-app","content":"Get the app"},"175":{"id":"/docs/install-4","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#check-the-download-optional","content":"Check the download (optional)"},"176":{"id":"/docs/install-5","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#move-it-to-applications","content":"Move it to Applications"},"177":{"id":"/docs/install-6","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#open-it-the-first-time","content":"Open it the first time"},"178":{"id":"/docs/install-7","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#try-to-open-it","content":"Try to open it"},"179":{"id":"/docs/install-8","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#open-privacy--security","content":"Open Privacy & Security"},"180":{"id":"/docs/install-9","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#allow-it","content":"Allow it"},"181":{"id":"/docs/install-10","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#give-it-full-disk-access","content":"Give it Full Disk Access"},"182":{"id":"/docs/install-11","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#open-the-setting","content":"Open the setting"},"183":{"id":"/docs/install-12","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#add-reclaim","content":"Add Reclaim"},"184":{"id":"/docs/install-13","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#scan-again","content":"Scan again"},"185":{"id":"/docs/install-14","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#updating","content":"Updating"},"186":{"id":"/docs/install-15","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#uninstalling","content":"Uninstalling"},"187":{"id":"/docs/install-16","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#remove-the-helper","content":"Remove the helper"},"188":{"id":"/docs/install-17","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#remove-the-app","content":"Remove the app"},"189":{"id":"/docs/install-18","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#remove-its-settings-and-history-optional","content":"Remove its settings and history (optional)"},"190":{"id":"/docs/install-19","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#tidy-up-permissions","content":"Tidy up permissions"},"191":{"id":"/docs/install-20","page_id":"/docs/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/install#build-from-source","content":"Build from source"},"192":{"id":"/docs/install-21","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#install-from-terminal","content":"The quickest way, and macOS opens Reclaim straight away with no warning. Paste this into Terminal:"},"193":{"id":"/docs/install-22","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#install-from-terminal","content":"It downloads the latest `Reclaim.dmg`, checks it against its published checksum, copies Reclaim into Applications and opens it. Run it again any time to update. You can read the script first."},"194":{"id":"/docs/install-23","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#install-from-terminal","content":"<Callout>Apps downloaded in a browser are marked as quarantined, and macOS checks them with Apple before they open. Files downloaded with `curl` are not marked, so there is nothing to allow.</Callout>"},"195":{"id":"/docs/install-24","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#get-the-app","content":"Download Reclaim.dmg, the latest version, ready to run: there is nothing to build. The release page also has `Reclaim.dmg.sha256` to check it, and the same app as `Reclaim.zip`."},"196":{"id":"/docs/install-25","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#check-the-download-optional","content":"In Terminal, in the folder you downloaded to:"},"197":{"id":"/docs/install-26","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#check-the-download-optional","content":"It should print `Reclaim.dmg: OK`."},"198":{"id":"/docs/install-27","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#move-it-to-applications","content":"Double-click `Reclaim.dmg` and drag **Reclaim** onto the **Applications** folder in the window that opens. Then eject the disk image in Finder."},"199":{"id":"/docs/install-28","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#open-it-the-first-time","content":"If you used the disk image: Reclaim is not notarized by Apple, because notarization needs a paid developer membership, so macOS blocks it the first time with *\"Apple could not verify… is free of malware\"*. You do this once per version."},"200":{"id":"/docs/install-29","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#open-it-the-first-time","content":"The quickest fix is one Terminal command, run before you open the disk image, that removes the quarantine mark macOS put on the download:"},"201":{"id":"/docs/install-30","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#open-it-the-first-time","content":"Or allow it in System Settings:"},"202":{"id":"/docs/install-31","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#try-to-open-it","content":"Double-click `Reclaim.dmg` (or Reclaim in Applications). macOS says it cannot verify it. Click **Done**, not Move to Trash."},"203":{"id":"/docs/install-32","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#open-privacy--security","content":"Go to **System Settings › Privacy & Security** and scroll to the Security section."},"204":{"id":"/docs/install-33","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#allow-it","content":"Next to the message about Reclaim, click **Open Anyway** and confirm with your password or Touch ID. If you allowed the disk image, macOS asks once more for the app itself the first time you open it from Applications: repeat these steps."},"205":{"id":"/docs/install-34","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#allow-it","content":"<Callout>The source is public, so you can also build it yourself instead of trusting a download.</Callout>"},"206":{"id":"/docs/install-35","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#give-it-full-disk-access","content":"Without it, macOS asks for permission the first time any app opens Desktop, Documents, Downloads, iCloud Drive or another app's data, and the app has to wait for your answer. To keep scans from stalling, Reclaim skips those folders until it has Full Disk Access, and the Overview says so, with a button to the right settings page."},"207":{"id":"/docs/install-36","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#open-the-setting","content":"Go to **System Settings › Privacy & Security › Full Disk Access**."},"208":{"id":"/docs/install-37","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#add-reclaim","content":"Click **+**, choose **Reclaim** in Applications, and make sure its switch is on."},"209":{"id":"/docs/install-38","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#scan-again","content":"Quit and reopen Reclaim, then scan."},"210":{"id":"/docs/install-39","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#scan-again","content":"No app can grant this to itself, and Reclaim never asks again once it is on."},"211":{"id":"/docs/install-40","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#scan-again","content":"<Callout>Your Music, TV and Photos libraries are always skipped, even with Full Disk Access, because macOS protects them with permissions of their own. Reclaim never suggests anything inside them.</Callout>"},"212":{"id":"/docs/install-41","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#updating","content":"Download the new release and replace the old app in Applications. Because each build is signed separately, macOS may ask you to repeat **Open Anyway**, you may need to switch Full Disk Access off and on again, and the helper, if you use it, asks to be paired again."},"213":{"id":"/docs/install-42","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#remove-the-helper","content":"If you installed it: open **System** in the sidebar and click **Remove Helper…**."},"214":{"id":"/docs/install-43","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#remove-the-app","content":"Quit Reclaim and move it from Applications to the Trash."},"215":{"id":"/docs/install-44","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#tidy-up-permissions","content":"Remove it from **Full Disk Access** and, if you turned it on, from **Login Items** in System Settings."},"216":{"id":"/docs/install-45","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#build-from-source","content":"You need Xcode and XcodeGen."},"217":{"id":"/docs/install-46","page_id":"/docs/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/install#build-from-source","content":"The engine's tests run with `swift test` in `Packages/ReclaimCore`. They only ever create and delete files in temporary folders."},"218":{"id":"/docs/settings","page_id":"/docs/settings","type":"page","content":"Settings","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/settings"},"219":{"id":"/docs/settings-0","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings","content":"Every Reclaim setting explained, from Trash mode and scan scope to thresholds, excluded folders, the menu bar, schedules, auto-clean, low-space alerts and accent colour."},"220":{"id":"/docs/settings-1","page_id":"/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/settings#general","content":"General"},"221":{"id":"/docs/settings-2","page_id":"/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/settings#scanning","content":"Scanning"},"222":{"id":"/docs/settings-3","page_id":"/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/settings#automation","content":"Automation"},"223":{"id":"/docs/settings-4","page_id":"/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/settings#appearance","content":"Appearance"},"224":{"id":"/docs/settings-5","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings","content":"Open Settings with **Reclaim › Settings…** or ⌘ ,. Changes apply at once unless noted."},"225":{"id":"/docs/settings-6","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#general","content":"| Setting                                       | What it does                                                                                                                                           | Default |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------- |\n| Move to Trash instead of deleting permanently | Ticked items go to the Trash, so you can put them back. Space is freed only when you empty it. Items that need the helper are left alone in this mode. | Off     |","table":"table-0"},"226":{"id":"/docs/settings-7","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#general","content":"| Setting                         | What it does                                                                            | Default |\n| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| Tick Safe items after each scan | Safe items are ticked as soon as a scan finishes. Rebuild and Personal items never are. | On      |","table":"table-0"},"227":{"id":"/docs/settings-8","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#general","content":"| Setting                  | What it does                       | Default |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ------- |\n| Restore Default Settings | Resets every setting on every tab. | —       |","table":"table-0"},"228":{"id":"/docs/settings-9","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#scanning","content":"| Setting | What it does                                                                                                       | Default    |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------