d":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#open-system","content":"Click **System** in the sidebar, then **Install Helper…**."},"262":{"id":"/docs/system-16","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#enter-your-password","content":"macOS asks in its own dialog. Reclaim never sees it."},"263":{"id":"/docs/system-17","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#enter-your-password","content":"The helper is copied to `/Library/PrivilegedHelperTools` and started by macOS whenever Reclaim needs it. After that, deleting works as usual: anything Reclaim may not delete is passed to the helper automatically when deleting permanently. In Move to Trash mode, such items are left alone."},"264":{"id":"/docs/system-18","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#what-keeps-it-safe","content":"<Card title=\"Fixed folders only\" description=\"System cache and log folders and your own home folder, after resolving symlinks. Never a protected f…\" />"},"265":{"id":"/docs/system-19","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#what-keeps-it-safe","content":"<Card title=\"No path tricks\" description=\"Paths with .. are refused, and so is a folder swapped for a link at the last moment.\" />"},"266":{"id":"/docs/system-20","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#what-keeps-it-safe","content":"<Card title=\"One app only\" description=\"Paired with the exact build of Reclaim that installed it. Any other program is refused.\" />"},"267":{"id":"/docs/system-21","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#what-keeps-it-safe","content":"<Card title=\"Open source\" href=\"https://github.com/kstmostofa/reclaim\" description=\"The helper is small, and its rules are tested. Read it on GitHub.\" />"},"268":{"id":"/docs/system-22","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#after-updating-reclaim","content":"The pairing names one exact build, so after an update the helper refuses the new version. **System** then shows **Pair Again…**, which asks for your password once more. A paid Apple developer certificate would remove this step."},"269":{"id":"/docs/system-23","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#local-time-machine-snapshots","content":"Time Machine keeps snapshots on your Mac's disk between backups, and they hold on to the space of files you deleted since. System lists them; with the helper installed you can tick and delete them. Backups on your backup disk are not affected, and macOS also removes local snapshots on its own when space runs low."},"270":{"id":"/docs/system-24","page_id":"/docs/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/system#removing-the-helper","content":"Click **Remove Helper…** in System and enter your password. Everything else in Reclaim keeps working without it."},"271":{"id":"/docs/what-it-finds","page_id":"/docs/what-it-finds","type":"page","content":"What it finds","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-finds"},"272":{"id":"/docs/what-it-finds-0","page_id":"/docs/what-it-finds","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-finds","content":"Every folder Reclaim suggests deleting on a Mac, including .next, node_modules, vendor, DerivedData, Gradle, npm and pip caches, Docker and system junk."},"273":{"id":"/docs/what-it-finds-1","page_id":"/docs/what-it-finds","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-finds#build-caches","content":"Build caches"},"274":{"id":"/docs/what-it-finds-2","page_id":"/docs/what-it-finds","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-finds#dependencies","content":"Dependencies"},"275":{"id":"/docs/what-it-finds-3","page_id":"/docs/what-it-finds","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-finds#package-caches","content":"Package caches"},"276":{"id":"/docs/what-it-finds-4","page_id":"/docs/what-it-finds","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs