96,"269":304,"270":152,"271":314,"272":173,"273":145,"274":157,"275":252,"276":138,"277":228,"278":139,"279":306,"280":219,"281":161,"282":286,"283":231,"284":176,"285":251,"286":101,"287":108,"288":97,"289":111,"290":118,"291":110,"292":98,"293":106,"294":99,"295":92,"296":104,"297":253,"298":114,"299":105,"300":125,"301":93,"302":44,"303":170,"304":124,"305":121,"306":120,"307":123,"308":112,"309":90,"310":102,"311":109,"312":91,"313":113,"314":96,"315":100,"316":122,"317":126,"318":201,"319":95,"320":94,"321":103,"322":107,"323":184,"324":116,"325":117,"326":180,"327":188,"328":229,"329":115,"330":119,"331":135,"332":186,"333":333,"334":257},"orderedDocs":[[54,"**Badges** mark folders a rule already suggests. A lock means a folder could not be read, so its size is a lower bound."],[145,"**Belongs to another user**, such as root: files created with `sudo` or by the system. The helper can delete these."],[60,"**By full contents.** Only the candidates left are read in full and compared by SHA-256. On a typical Mac this takes seconds."],[58,"**By size.** Files with a unique size cannot have a twin, so they are dropped first."],[59,"**By their edges.** The first and last 64 KB of the remaining files are compared."],[12,"**Clean Safe Items** deletes every Safe suggestion Reclaim can delete, then shows a notification with the space freed."],[10,"**Free space** and a small storage bar, with what the last scan found."],[52,"**Go back:** click any folder in the trail at the top, or press ⌘ ↑."],[51,"**Go deeper:** double-click a folder, or right-click it and choose **Open**."],[167,"**Hard limits.** System folders, your home folder and folders like Documents are never deleted as a whole, however the path is written."],[65,"**Hard links** are one file with several names, so they never appear as duplicates. **APFS copies**, such as those made with Finder's Duplicate, can share storage with the original. Reclaim detects them from where their data sits on disk and marks them *Shares storage*. Deleting one frees almost nothing, so they don't count towards the reclaimable total."],[164,"**It explains everything.** Every suggestion says what it is, why it is listed and what happens after you delete it."],[146,"**It no longer exists:** something else removed it after the scan."],[67,"**Keep Oldest Copy** or **Keep Newest Copy**, by modification date."],[68,"**Keep the Copy in a Folder…**: in groups with a copy in the folder you choose, that copy is kept."],[130,"**Last scan:** how much you could reclaim, how much of it is Safe, and how long the scan took."],[259,"**Local Time Machine snapshots**."],[166,"**No nagging.** Tick, click, done, with a summary of anything that could not be removed."],[126,"**One disk only.** External drives and other volumes are never scanned."],[13,"**Open Reclaim**, Settings and Quit."],[168,"**Private.** No account, no analytics, no network access. The source is on GitHub."],[147,"**Protected:** one of the folders Reclaim never deletes as a whole. See the FAQ."],[125,"**Real sizes.** Reclaim counts the space files actually use. A 32 GB disk image holding 1 GB counts as 1 GB, and a file with several hard links counts once."],[135,"**Right-click** rows to tick or untick several at once, or to reveal one in Finder."],[258,"**Root-owned files in your home folder**, such as those left by `sudo npm install`."],[11,"**Scan Now** starts a scan without opening the window."],[134,"**Select All Safe** ticks every Safe item in the list; **Deselect All** unticks the list."],[55,"**Small files** under 1 MB are not listed one by one; their total appears below the list."],[133,"**Sort** by clicking a column header, and **filter** with the search field (⌘ F)."],[129,"**Storage bar:** used space, the part Reclaim suggests deleting in your accent colour, and free space."],[256,"**System caches** in `/Library/Caches`."],[257,"**System logs** in `/Library/Logs` and `/private/var/log`."],[136,"**The inspector** on the right explains the selected item: what it is, why it is suggested, what happens after deleting it, and where it is."],[165,"**Three safety levels.** <Level of=\"safe\" /> items rebuild themselves and are ticked for you. <Level of=\"rebuild\" /> and <Level of=\"personal\" /> items wait for your decision."],[53,"**Tick anything** that is not protected. Protected folders, such as the top level of the disk or your home folder, have a dimmed checkbox."],[131,"**Top categories:** each kind of suggestion with its size. Click one to open it."],[69,"**Untick All Copies**."],[124,"**Whole disk by default.** To scan only your home folder, change Scanning › Scan."],[127,"**Without Full Disk Access**, Desktop, Documents, Downloads, iCloud Drive and other apps' data are skipped, so macOS doesn't pause the scan to ask about each one. Turn it on."],[37,"<Callout type=\"success\">Ticked items are removed with Docker's own commands, never forced, so Docker itself refuses anything a container is using. Reclaim never touches the engine's disk image directly.</Callout>"],[143,"<Callout type=\"warn\" title=\"There is no confirmation\">The button, or ⌘ ⌫, deletes ticked items immediately and permanently. For a safety net, turn on Move to Trash instead of deleting permanently; space is then freed only when you empty the Trash.</Callout>"],[137,"<Callout type=\"warn\">An orange warning next to an app's cache means that app is running; quit it before deleting its files. A lock means the item belongs to root, and deleting it needs the helper.</Callout>"],[71,"<Callout type=\"warn\">If every copy in a group is ticked, the group shows a warning: deleting them all leaves you with none.</Callout>"],[194,"<Callout>Apps downloaded in a browser are marked as quarantined, and macOS checks them with Apple before they open. Files downloaded with `curl` are not marked, so there is nothing to allow.</Callout>"],[302,"<Callout>Packages that tools installed for themselves are skipped: anything in a hidden folder in your home (such as `~/.vscode/extensions` or `~/.composer`), in `~/Library`, or in system and Homebrew locations. Deleting those would break the tool, and there is no project to reinstall into.</Callout>"],[205,"<Callout>The source is public, so you can also build it yourself instead of trusting a download.</Callout>"],[211,"<Callout>Your Music, TV and Photos libraries are always skipped, even with Full Disk Access, because macOS protects them with permissions of their own. Reclaim never suggests anything inside them.</Callout>"],[163,"<Card title=\"FAQ\" href=\"/docs/faq\" description=\"Safety, permissions, sizes and privacy.\" />"],[264,"<Card title=\"Fixed folders only\" description=\"System cache and log folders and your own home folder, after resolving symlinks. Never a protected f…\" />"],[160,"<Card title=\"Install\" href=\"/docs/install\" description=\"Download, open it the first time, and give it Full Disk Access.\" />"],[265,"<Card title=\"No path tricks\" description=\"Paths with .. are refused, and so is a folder swapped for a link at the last moment.\" />"],[266,"<Card title=\"One app only\" description=\"Paired with the exact build of Reclaim that installed it. Any other program is refused.\" />"],[267,"<Card title=\"Open source\" href=\"https://github.com/kstmostofa/reclaim\" description=\"The helper is small, and its rules are tested. Read it on GitHub.\" />"],[161,"<Card title=\"Scan and clean\" href=\"/docs/guide\" description=\"Your first scan, the safety levels, and deleting.\" />"],[162,"<Card title=\"What it finds\" href=\"/docs/what-it-finds\" description=\"Every rule, with its safety level.\" />"],[49,"<Screenshot src=\"disk-map.png\" dark=\"dark-disk-map.png\" alt=\"The Disk Map listing folders with size bars, sizes, their share of the parent folder and file counts…\" />"],[9,"<Screenshot src=\"menu-bar.png\" dark=\"dark-menu-bar.png\" narrow alt=\"The Reclaim menu-bar window with free space, a storage bar, the last scan and Scan Now and Clean Saf…\" />"],[128,"<Screenshot src=\"overview.png\" alt=\"Overview with a storage bar, the last scan's summary and the top categories.\" />"],[241,"<Screenshot src=\"settings-appearance.png\" dark=\"dark-settings-appearance.png\" narrow alt=\"Appearance settings: system, light or dark, accent colour swatches, custom colour and a preview.\" />"],[234,"<Screenshot src=\"settings-automation.png\" dark=\"dark-settings-automation.png\" narrow alt=\"Automation settings: menu bar, open at login, scheduled scans, auto-clean and low-space alerts.\" />"],[34,"| Item              | What it is                                                        | Removed with          | Level   |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------- |\n| Stopped container | A container that is not running. Changes made inside it are lost. | `docker container rm` | <Level of=\"rebuild\" /> |"],[32,"| Item           | What it is                                                     | Removed with      | Level   |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- | ------- |\n| Dangling image | An untagged image left behind when a newer build took its tag. | `docker image rm` | <Level of=\"safe\" /> |"],[35,"| Item          | What it is                                              | Removed with       | Level   |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------- |\n| Unused volume | A volume no container uses. These often hold databases. | `docker volume rm` | <Level of=\"personal\" /> |"],[33,"| Item         | What it is                                                           | Removed with      | Level   |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- | ------- |\n| Unused image | A tagged image no container uses. Pulled or built again when needed. | `docker image rm` | <Level of=\"rebuild\" /> |"],[31,"| Item        | What it is                                                 | Removed with                 | Level   |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------- |\n| Build cache | Layers kept to speed up builds, not used by any image now. | `docker builder prune --all` | <Level of=\"safe\" /> |"],[138,"| Level   | Meaning                                                                                                | Ticked for you |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------- |\n| <Level of=\"safe\" /> | Rebuilds itself; nothing for you to do. Build caches, app caches, logs, emulator snapshots, the Trash. | Yes            |"],[140,"| Level   | Meaning                                                                                            | Ticked for you |\n| ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| <Level of=\"personal\" /> | Your data, reported so you can decide: old downloads, large files, duplicates, emulator user data. | No             |"],[139,"| Level   | Meaning                                                                                | Ticked for you |\n| ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| <Level of=\"rebuild\" /> | Comes back after a reinstall or download, such as `npm install` or `composer install`. | No             |"],[225,"| Setting                                       | What it does                                                                                                                                           | Default |\n| --------------------------------------------- | -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------